components.responsibility:
A default-suite Fact on real temp trees through Scans.RunCancellingAt, sweeping the stopping call k before and during the call. Checks:
- whenever OffersStoppedTree is true: store.Count > 0, NotListed(0) is false and ChildCount(0) agrees with TopLevel's row count;
- whenever the store is empty or the root is NotListed: OffersStoppedTree is false;
- a Completed result is never offered.

It also pins that no entry of a stopped store is both NotListed and in result.Unreadable. The note arms' order relies on that.

New file.

StopAt(app, window, target):
- arms on the hook thread before the scan starts and waits for MainWindow._progress to be non-null;
- spins with a Stopwatch/SpinWait loop, never Thread.Sleep, over a volatile read of ScanProgress's raw _currentFolder, calling CurrentFolder only when the reference changes, as spike 120 did (44 ns a read);
- matches root\target exactly when the target has no trailing backslash, and root\target or anything under it when it does;
- on the first match, posts at DispatcherPriority.Send a callback that raises ButtonBase.ClickEvent on CancelButton if StartupHook.Pressable allows;
- logs `tree-stop target seen pressedAt detectToCallbackUs pollMeanNs worstGapMs ms`, where pressedAt is CurrentFolder at callback entry, the last committed folder;
- logs `tree-stop refused reason=ended-first` if the scan ends first.

Choose(window) sets ShowTreeButton.IsChecked = true, settles at ContextIdle and logs `tree-chosen` (tree, list, header).

There is no warm-up scan: spike 120 measured it at +0.33 s for the same 20/20 cut.

Records the following:
- the person-asked stopped tree supersedes docs/design/SL-044-folder-tree.md's 'a stopped scan shows no tree' (lines 11-16);
- why the list stays the default (Q-273; only the list can say 'stopped partway');
- the one-word rule and the HasFigures gate;
- OffersStoppedTree;
- spike 120's finding that CurrentFolder names the last committed folder, which is how a cut is spelled;
- Q-275's unattended R-004;
- the named residuals: a listed folder holding unread folders shows short figures with no note (no subtree-unfinished mark), and a Stop-cut folder cannot be told from a queued one (U-189).

